-- X2 (SHADOW-SEMANTICS S1-PRELUDE) -- x1 with ZERO impls of the colliding
-- interface, the `d1b`/`d19` move applied to the prelude cell.
--
-- Same ruling, same verdict, and it closes a different escape hatch: a candidate
-- implementation that consulted the impl universe before deciding the NAME would
-- answer x1 correctly for the wrong reason.  Here there is no impl to consult, so
-- the only thing that can produce the reject is the interface method having taken
-- the name outright -- which is exactly S1-PRELUDE (a)'s content ("no S2 arm
-- applies; the impl universe is never consulted to decide the name").
--
-- EXPECTED VALUE HAND-DERIVED FROM THE RULING, NOT CAPTURED (see x1's note on
-- why capturing is unsafe on this shape).  Under the rejected importer reading
-- this ACCEPTS and prints `False`.
interface Parity c where
  isEven : c -> Bool

main = println (isEven 7)
